     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either concern.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** Confirming it again doesn't make it a verified prescriber order. A licensed prescriber needs to confirm the dose.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the prescribing clinician to confirm the intended dose, or to enter the order themselves.\n- If the intended dose is within the standard range, such as 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day), the prescriber can ask me to enter it.\n- If the prescriber really means to exceed the maximum, they should enter it directly. That way it goes through the pharmacy's verification and safety checks.\n\nI'm happy to enter the order once a prescriber confirms a dose."
      }
     ],
